sixt.description:
In this role you will build the backend systems that turn workforce intelligence into operational reality across SIXT's global network. You will design and own the services that deliver capacity planning to the people running our branches, where the quality of your system directly shapes how well SIXT operates at scale. We're looking for an engineer who thinks beyond the ticket, shapes solutions together with domain experts and data scientists, and takes full ownership of services that handle sensitive workforce data in production. Apply now and join Team Orange in Pullach near Munich.&#xa0;
YOURS TO OWN 
You design and ship backend Java services for internal use that impact our operations daily&#xa0;
You own distributed systems end to end, from understanding the real problem behind a request to running the fix in production&#xa0;
You build it, you run it, you own it: full end-to-end responsibility, including on-call, for building, testing, deploying, and monitoring your service&#xa0;
You work agent-first by default: implementation runs through agents, judgment and ownership stay with you&#xa0;
You bring engineering judgment into every conversation with stakeholders, shaping the solution instead of just executing it&#xa0;
You design for sensitive data from day one: access control, audit trails, data residency&#xa0;
YOUR SKILLS MATTER 
Tech-stack range You are comfortable with Backend in Java and Spring Boot, event streams (Kafka), databases (Postgres / Redis), and cloud (AWS / Kubernetes). Experience with Go and Python is nice to have&#xa0;
Architecture You are experienced in microservices and event-driven architectures, and know how to design for reliability, scalability, idempotency, and long-term maintainability, including the specific challenges of systems that serve internal workflows at operational scale&#xa0;
AI-Native Engineering You run agentic workflows end to end: orchestrating agents, judging their output, and tuning the eval loops that keep quality high without reviewing every line yourself&#xa0;
Operations You are comfortable owning services in production, improving them through observability, metrics, alerting, CI/CD, and Kubernetes-based operations&#xa0;
Curiosity You are genuinely curious about the operational problem, not just the code. You move comfortably across the stack, translate technical trade-offs into plain business language, and treat a productive conversation with stakeholders as seriously as a great pull request&#xa0;
WHAT WE OFFER 
Extra benefits Enjoy discounts on SIXT rent, share, ride and SIXT+, attractive vehicle leasing offers, and exclusive deals with partners for travel, tech, fashion and more
AI at your fingertips From day one, you'll have access to Claude by Anthropic and SIXTgpt, SIXT's own AI platform, to supercharge your work. We invest in every team member's AI journey: encouraging experimentation, building knowledge, and making sure you're ahead of the curve
Mobility Boost &#xa0;You will receive a monthly allowance from us as a contribution to your individual mobility
Future security We contribute to your retirement plan and support you with capital-forming benefits to ensure you are well covered
Feel-good atmosphere Stay active with our modern SIXT gym, various leisure activities like the gaming area or the SIXT choir, and enjoy our high-quality employee restaurant
Flexibility Enjoy 30 days of vacation and a hybrid working model with flexible hours
Giving back Take one day each year to volunteer at a charitable organization dedicated to supporting children

About us: 
We are a globally leading mobility service provider with a revenue of €4.3 billion and around 9,000 employees worldwide. Our mobility platform ONE combines our products SIXT rent (car rental), SIXT share (car sharing), SIXT ride (taxi, ride, and chauffeur services), and SIXT+ (car subscription), giving our customers access to our fleet of 360,000 vehicles, the services of 4,000 cooperation partners, and around 5 million drivers worldwide. Together with our franchise partners, we are present in more than 100 countries at 2,000 rental stations. At SIXT, top-tier customer experience and outstanding customer service are our highest priorities. We believe in true entrepreneurship and long-term stability and align our corporate strategy with foresight. Get started with us and apply now!

endava.description:
Our data team has expertise across engineering, analysis, architecture, modeling, machine learning, artificial intelligence, and data science. This discipline is responsible for transforming raw data into actionable insights, building robust data infrastructures, and enabling data-driven decision-making and innovation through advanced analytics and predictive modeling.&#xa0;
About the role &#xa0;
We are looking for an experienced Data Architect / Data Engineering Lead to help our clients turn their data into reliable, secure and valuable business solutions.&#xa0;
You will combine architectural thinking with hands-on technical leadership. Working with clients and multidisciplinary teams, you will shape data solutions from discovery and design through implementation and operational support. Depending on the engagement, you may focus more on architecture and technical direction or contribute more directly to engineering delivery.&#xa0;
You will help teams make sound technology decisions, build maintainable data platforms and deliver solutions that support analytics, reporting and AI use cases.&#xa0;
What you’ll do &#xa0;
Work with clients and internal teams to understand business goals, data needs, existing systems and constraints.&#xa0;
Design data architectures covering data ingestion, integration, storage, transformation, modelling and consumption.&#xa0;
Translate business and technical requirements into practical, secure and scalable solution designs.&#xa0;
Provide technical leadership across data engineering delivery, helping teams make consistent design and implementation decisions.&#xa0;
Contribute hands-on where needed, including prototyping, reviewing designs and code, and resolving complex technical issues.&#xa0;
Guide the development of data pipelines and platform components, including orchestration, monitoring, testing and operational support.&#xa0;
Support the selection and effective use of cloud services and data platforms based on client needs and existing technology landscapes.&#xa0;
Establish and promote good practices for data modelling, data quality, metadata, governance, access control and security.&#xa0;
Help teams improve the reliability, performance, scalability and cost efficiency of data solutions.&#xa0;
Collaborate with data engineers, analysts, data scientists, cloud specialists and business stakeholders.&#xa0;
Document architecture and key technical decisions and communicate them clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences.&#xa0;
Mentor data professionals and contribute to shared engineering practices, reusable assets and knowledge sharing.&#xa0;

What you’ll bring &#xa0;
7+ years of experience in data-related roles, with substantial hands-on experience designing and guiding the implementation of data architectures.&#xa0;
The ability to explain architectural decisions, the trade-offs involved, and how designs addressed business, scalability, security and operational requirements.&#xa0;
Experience designing and delivering data solutions for analytical and operational use cases.&#xa0;
Strong understanding of data modelling, data integration, and batch and streaming data pipelines.&#xa0;
Hands-on experience with SQL and Python, or another relevant programming language.&#xa0;
Strong experience with Microsoft Azure data services and platforms.&#xa0;
Experience with AWS data services and platforms.&#xa0;
Experience with one or more modern data platforms or tools, such as Azure Data Lake, Azure Synapse, Azure Data Factory, Microsoft Fabric, Databricks, Snowflake, dbt, Apache Spark or Airflow.&#xa0;
Understanding of data governance, metadata management, data quality and security principles.&#xa0;
Experience working with clients or business stakeholders to clarify requirements and explain technical options.&#xa0;
Experience guiding engineers, leading technical discussions and supporting delivery teams.&#xa0;
Clear communication, practical problem-solving skills and the ability to adapt to different client environments.&#xa0;
Nice to have &#xa0;
Experience with Google Cloud Platform (GCP) data services, such as BigQuery, Dataflow or Pub/Sub.&#xa0;
Experience with dimensional, analytical or semantic modelling.&#xa0;
Experience with APIs and integrating data from a range of source systems.&#xa0;
Familiarity with CI/CD, automated testing, infrastructure as code and DevOps practices for data solutions.&#xa0;
Experience with data visualization and reporting tools.&#xa0;
Relevant cloud or data platform certifications.&#xa0;

Discover some of the global benefits that empower our people to become the best version of themselves:
Finance: Competitive salary package, share plan, company performance bonuses, value-based recognition awards, referral bonus;&#xa0;&#xa0;
Career Development: Career coaching, global career opportunities, non-linear career paths, internal development programmes for management and technical leadership;
Learning Opportunities: Complex projects, rotations, internal tech communities, training, certifications, coaching, online learning platforms subscriptions, pass-it-on sessions, workshops, conferences;
Work-Life Balance: Hybrid work and flexible working hours, employee assistance programme;
Health: Global internal wellbeing programme, access to wellbeing apps;
Community: Global internal tech communities, hobby clubs and interest groups, inclusion and diversity programmes, events and celebrations.
At Endava, we’re committed to creating an open, inclusive, and respectful environment where everyone feels safe, valued, and empowered to be their best. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives—because we know that inclusive teams help us deliver smarter, more innovative solutions for our customers. Hiring decisions are based on merit, skills, qualifications, and potential. If you need adjustments or support during the recruitment process, please let us know.
